<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Web Programming FAQ</title></head>
<body>
<section id="faq">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <details open>
    <summary>What is HTML?</summary>
    <p>HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard language for
       structuring content on web pages.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What is the difference between &lt;section&gt; and &lt;article&gt;?</summary>
    <p>A <strong>section</strong> groups related content in context. An
       <strong>article</strong> stands alone and can be published independently.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Why is the alt attribute important?</summary>
    <p>It gives images alternative text for screen readers and for when
       the image fails to load.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What does DOCTYPE do?</summary>
    <p>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt; tells the browser to use standards mode for
       consistent rendering.</p>
  </details>
</section>
</body>
</html>
